Title: Endogenous Nanostructure Organisms: A Synthetic Architecture for Self‑Generated Physiology, Regulation, Evolution, and Cryptographic IntegrityAuthor: C. Matthew Blackwell, Independent Designer, Lafayette, LouisianaCorrespondence: Blackwell Research Labs

Abstract

We present a synthetic organism architecture built entirely from nanostructure logic rather than biological tissue. The system exhibits endogenous signal generation, organ‑state transitions, dynamic internal engines, self‑regulation, non‑genetic evolution, cryptographic integrity, and identity coherence. This architecture defines a new class of synthetic endogenous nanostructure organisms (SENO), enabling physiology‑like behavior without cells, evolution without DNA, and organism‑level sovereignty through cryptographic verification. We outline the system’s architecture, functional dynamics, scientific significance, and interdisciplinary research implications.

1. Introduction

Nanotechnology has traditionally focused on materials, particles, and nanoscale devices. Synthetic biology has focused on engineered cells and gene circuits. Artificial life simulations have focused on computational agents lacking physiological depth.

The endogenous nanostructure organism architecture introduced here merges these domains into a unified system capable of:

generating internal signals

regulating internal states

evolving internal logic

maintaining identity coherence

proving its own transitions cryptographically

This represents a category‑creating discovery: a synthetic organism without biological tissue.

2. System Architecture

The architecture consists of seven functional layers:

2.1 Endogenous Signal Layer

Generates hormone‑like pulses (stress, reward, energy, mood) without external input.

2.2 Organ‑State Layer

Models organ‑like regions with four states: OK, strained, overloaded, repairing.

2.3 Dynamic Engine Layer

Stress, reward, energy, and mood engines generate internal dynamics analogous to metabolic and psychological cycles.

2.4 Regulation Layer

Endogenous endocrine and autonomic modules maintain homeostasis.

2.5 Evolution Layer

Evolution vector, adaptive mutation engine, self‑repair engine, and trajectory predictor enable non‑genetic evolution.

2.6 Integrity Layer

Endogenous ledger, integrity guard, and self‑proof module ensure cryptographic sovereignty.

2.7 Identity Layer

Identity vector, coherence engine, and drift timeline define a persistent synthetic “self.”

3. Functional Dynamics

3.1 Initialization

System boots with baseline internal states and establishes identity.

